WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.333
The best visualization starts with an analyst question.

00:00:03.333 --> 00:00:06.667
Pivotglass offers twelve evidence views, each with a stated scope,

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:10.000
a reason for the chart, and exact data. Let us look at the

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.333
same synthetic case through several lenses. Relationship graphs expose
typed

00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:16.667
connections. Provenance history preserves admissions and

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:20.000
analyst grouping. Connection counts identify dense neighborhoods for

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.333
inspection. Graph position and node degree do not establish

00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:26.667
maliciousness or common control. Stored-type

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:30.000
charts summarize the inventory. Dossier completeness and the

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.333
constellation expose gaps. Activity views

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:36.667
separate investigation records from enrichment task state. Coverage

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:40.000
similarity compares evidence profiles, not actor identity.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.333
Empty or unavailable dimensions remain visible instead of

00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:46.667
being guessed. The competing-hypotheses matrix projects explicit

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:50.000
support and contradiction links. Here, the same connected

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.333
cluster supports both explanations. That overlap is the

00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:56.667
interesting part: it does not discriminate. Unassessed

00:00:56.667 --> 00:01:00.000
cells have no recorded stance. Open exact data to

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.333
inspect rationales and mixed evidence. A structured technique run

00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:06.667
records the method, selected inputs, findings, limitations,

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:10.000
and disposition. In this demonstration, a key

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.333
assumptions check challenges the leap from shared infrastructure to
common

00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:16.667
control. Its result is an authored review and a collection need,

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:20.000
not automatic attribution.   The hierarchy organizes

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.333
questions and analytical records under the investigation. Likelihood

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:26.667
ranges and confidence history keep probability separate from the basis

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:30.000
for belief. Membership in a tree is organizational;

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.333
it is not a support link.   Bring it together in the deterministic

00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:36.667
report: questions, hypotheses, evidence links, technique

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:40.000
results, contradictions, and next steps. Save

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.333
editable Markdown or print to PDF. Export exact chart

00:01:43.333 --> 00:01:46.667
data when a reviewer needs the underlying rows. Use the visualization

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:49.933
to discover a question, and the report to make the reasoning
reviewable.
